message: "If you use PyCognition or the WebDrift-Fault-50 benchmark in your research, please cite it as below. / Wenn Sie PyCognition oder den Benchmark WebDrift-Fault-50 in Ihrer Forschung nutzen, zitieren Sie diese bitte wie folgt."
title: "PyCognition: Dual-Tier Neuro-Symbolic Cognitive Orchestration Framework with Telemetry-Driven Skill Refactoring"
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-12
authors:
  - family-names: "Riabtsev"
    given-names: "Oleh"
    affiliation: "Universität Vechta"
repository-code: "https://github.com/MasterUaKi/pycognition"
url: "https://github.com/MasterUaKi/pycognition"
license: "LGPL-3.0-or-later"
keywords:
  - "neuro-symbolic AI"
  - "cognitive orchestration"
  - "self-healing agents"
  - "skill crystallization"
  - "AST safety auditing"
  - "capability-based security"
  - "telemetry-driven refactoring"
  - "WebDrift-Fault-50"
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Grant Harvester: Autonomous Academic Funding Monitoring Framework with Cognitive Multi-Tier Reflection"
    authors:
      - family-names: "Riabtsev"
        given-names: "Oleh"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.24106395"
abstract: |
  PyCognition is a domain-agnostic neuro-symbolic orchestration framework pairing fast,
  deterministic System 1 procedural execution with deliberative System 2 LLM reflection.
  Version 1.2.0 introduces a closed-loop telemetry-driven skill refactoring subsystem
  (capability.py, telemetry.py, crystallizer.py) and the WebDrift-Fault-50 benchmark.
  By shifting feedback from data-level micro-patching to AST-audited, regression-guarded
  code synthesis, PyCognition eliminates toxic micro-compensation and database poisoning
  in non-stationary open web environments.
